  "what": "Path-sanitized public copies of A/B run receipts, bound by hash.",
  "why": "Sanitizing agent.argv[0] changed each receipt's bytes, so the self-digest each file carries no longer recomputes over it. The digests were deliberately NOT regenerated -- a regenerated digest would make a rewritten receipt look like one produced that way. This manifest binds what the public files actually are, and names the original bytes so the unmodified receipt is identifiable."
